IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `oas-core`
IMPORT `oas-core-measures`
IMPORT `oas-core-terms`
IMPORT `oa1-nouns`
IMPORT `oa1-part1-eligibility`

-- Tests of oa1-part1-eligibility. Every expected value is worked out from the text of the Act (the line of the
-- provision is in the comment), never read off the encoding's output. Approval day for every person: October 1, 2026.

-- The person-maker, positionally, in the order of the record `s 3: Facts of age and residence`:
--   born, approved, pensioner 1977, resided 1977, earlier residence, visa, ten years, presence before, absence during, one year, aggregate, resident preceding day
GIVEN born        IS A DATE
      approved    IS A DATE
      pensioner77 IS A BOOLEAN
      resided77   IS A BOOLEAN
      earlier     IS A BOOLEAN
      visa        IS A BOOLEAN
      tenYears    IS A BOOLEAN
      presence    IS A NUMBER
      absence     IS A NUMBER
      oneYear     IS A BOOLEAN
      aggregate   IS A NUMBER
      residentOnPrecedingDay IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 3: Facts of age and residence`
`oa1 test: person` born approved pensioner77 resided77 earlier visa tenYears presence absence oneYear aggregate residentOnPrecedingDay MEANS
    `s 3: Facts of age and residence` OF born, approved, pensioner77, resided77, earlier, visa, tenYears, presence, absence, oneYear, aggregate, residentOnPrecedingDay

`oa1 test: the day of approval` MEANS YMD 2026 10 1

§ `s 3(1): a full monthly pension`

-- (a) a pensioner on July 1, 1977 (line 97): qualified whatever else is true.
#ASSERT `s 3(1)(a): the person was a pensioner on July 1, 1977` (`oa1 test: person` (YMD 1940 1 1) `oa1 test: the day of approval` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE 0 FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 3(1): a full monthly pension may be paid to the person` (`oa1 test: person` (YMD 1940 1 1) `oa1 test: the day of approval` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE 0 FALSE)
-- A person not a pensioner in 1977 does not satisfy (a).
#ASSERT NOT (`s 3(1)(a): the person was a pensioner on July 1, 1977` (`oa1 test: person` (YMD 1950 3 1) `oa1 test: the day of approval` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 0 0 TRUE 50 TRUE))
-- A pensioner in 1977 is excluded from (b)(i) ("was not a pensioner") and from (c)(i).
#ASSERT NOT (`s 3(1)(b)(i): on July 1, 1977 the person was not a pensioner but had attained twenty-five years of age and met the test of residence` (`oa1 test: person` (YMD 1940 1 1) `oa1 test: the day of approval` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 0 0 TRUE 50 TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 3(1)(c): the person is qualified for a full monthly pension under paragraph (c)` (`oa1 test: person` (YMD 1940 1 1) `oa1 test: the day of approval` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 0 0 TRUE 50 TRUE))

-- (b): born March 1, 1950 is 27 on July 1, 1977 (at least 25), resided in Canada then, 76 on the day of approval, resided
-- the ten years immediately preceding: all of (i), (ii), (iii) hold (lines 98-101).
#ASSERT `s 3(1)(b): the person is qualified for a full monthly pension under paragraph (b)` (`oa1 test: person` (YMD 1950 3 1) `oa1 test: the day of approval` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 0 0 TRUE 50 TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 3(1): a full monthly pension may be paid to the person` (`oa1 test: person` (YMD 1950 3 1) `oa1 test: the day of approval` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 0 0 TRUE 50 TRUE)

-- (b)(i), the age edge: twenty-five years on July 1, 1977 means born on or before July 1, 1952.
#ASSERT `s 3(1)(b)(i): on July 1, 1977 the person was not a pensioner but had attained twenty-five years of age and met the test of residence` (`oa1 test: person` (YMD 1952 7 1) `oa1 test: the day of approval` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 0 0 TRUE 50 TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 3(1)(b)(i): on July 1, 1977 the person was not a pensioner but had attained twenty-five years of age and met the test of residence` (`oa1 test: person` (YMD 1952 7 2) `oa1 test: the day of approval` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 0 0 TRUE 50 TRUE))

-- (b)(i), the residence limb: resided in Canada on July 1, 1977 suffices; failing that, earlier residence after eighteen suffices; failing that, a valid visa suffices; none of them fails.
#ASSERT `s 3(1)(b)(i): on July 1, 1977 the person was not a pensioner but had attained twenty-five years of age and met the test of residence` (`oa1 test: person` (YMD 1950 3 1) `oa1 test: the day of approval` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 0 0 TRUE 50 TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 3(1)(b)(i): on July 1, 1977 the person was not a pensioner but had attained twenty-five years of age and met the test of residence` (`oa1 test: person` (YMD 1950 3 1) `oa1 test: the day of approval` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE 0 0 TRUE 50 TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 3(1)(b)(i): on July 1, 1977 the person was not a pensioner but had attained twenty-five years of age and met the test of residence` (`oa1 test: person` (YMD 1950 3 1) `oa1 test: the day of approval` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE 0 0 TRUE 50 TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 3(1)(b)(i): on July 1, 1977 the person was not a pensioner but had attained twenty-five years of age and met the test of residence` (`oa1 test: person` (YMD 1950 3 1) `oa1 test: the day of approval` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE 0 0 TRUE 50 TRUE))

-- (b)(ii) and 3(2)(a): sixty-five on the day of approval. Born October 1, 1961 is 65 on October 1, 2026; born October 2, 1961 is 64.
#ASSERT `s 3(1)(b)(ii): the person has attained sixty-five years of age` (`oa1 test: person` (YMD 1961 10 1) `oa1 test: the day of approval` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE 40 TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 3(1)(b)(ii): the person has attained sixty-five years of age` (`oa1 test: person` (YMD 1961 10 2) `oa1 test: the day of approval` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE 40 TRUE))

-- (b)(iii), second limb: not resident for the ten years; present 30 years against absences of 10 years is exactly three
-- times (at least equal), and one year's residence: qualifies. 29 years does not; no year's residence does not.
#ASSERT `s 3(1)(b)(iii): the person has resided in Canada for the ten years immediately preceding, or has been present for three times the absences and resided for one year` (`oa1 test: person` (YMD 1950 3 1) `oa1 test: the day of approval` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 30 10 TRUE 50 TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 3(1)(b)(iii): the person has resided in Canada for the ten years immediately preceding, or has been present for three times the absences and resided for one year` (`oa1 test: person` (YMD 1950 3 1) `oa1 test: the day of approval` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 29 10 TRUE 50 TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 3(1)(b)(iii): the person has resided in Canada for the ten years immediately preceding, or has been present for three times the absences and resided for one year` (`oa1 test: person` (YMD 1950 3 1) `oa1 test: the day of approval` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 30 10 FALSE 50 TRUE))
-- Resided the ten years: qualifies without the presence test.
#ASSERT `s 3(1)(b)(iii): the person has resided in Canada for the ten years immediately preceding, or has been present for three times the absences and resided for one year` (`oa1 test: person` (YMD 1950 3 1) `oa1 test: the day of approval` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 0 0 TRUE 50 TRUE)
-- The one-year clause belongs to the second limb (fork OA1-F2): a person who resided the ten years qualifies even where the one-year input is FALSE.
#ASSERT `s 3(1)(b)(iii): the person has resided in Canada for the ten years immediately preceding, or has been present for three times the absences and resided for one year` (`oa1 test: person` (YMD 1950 3 1) `oa1 test: the day of approval` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 0 0 FALSE 50 TRUE)
-- (b) as a whole fails when (iii) fails even though (i) and (ii) hold.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 3(1)(b): the person is qualified for a full monthly pension under paragraph (b)` (`oa1 test: person` (YMD 1950 3 1) `oa1 test: the day of approval` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 29 10 TRUE 50 TRUE))

-- (c): not a pensioner in 1977, sixty-five, and forty years of residence after eighteen (lines 102-105). Exactly 40 qualifies.
#ASSERT `s 3(1)(c): the person is qualified for a full monthly pension under paragraph (c)` (`oa1 test: person` (YMD 1961 10 1) `oa1 test: the day of approval` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE 40 TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 3(1): a full monthly pension may be paid to the person` (`oa1 test: person` (YMD 1961 10 1) `oa1 test: the day of approval` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE 40 TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 3(1)(c): the person is qualified for a full monthly pension under paragraph (c)` (`oa1 test: person` (YMD 1961 10 1) `oa1 test: the day of approval` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE 39.9 TRUE))
-- ... and not at sixty-four, however long the residence.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 3(1)(c): the person is qualified for a full monthly pension under paragraph (c)` (`oa1 test: person` (YMD 1961 10 2) `oa1 test: the day of approval` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE 45 TRUE))
-- A person born in 1961 cannot satisfy (b): not twenty-five in 1977.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 3(1): a full monthly pension may be paid to the person` (`oa1 test: person` (YMD 1961 10 1) `oa1 test: the day of approval` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE 0 0 TRUE 39 TRUE))

§ `s 3(2): a partial monthly pension`

-- Ten years is the least: 10 qualifies, 9.9 does not (line 109), with sixty-five and residence on the preceding day.
#ASSERT `s 3(2): a partial monthly pension may be paid to the person` (`oa1 test: person` (YMD 1961 10 1) `oa1 test: the day of approval` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE 10 TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 3(2): a partial monthly pension may be paid to the person` (`oa1 test: person` (YMD 1961 10 1) `oa1 test: the day of approval` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE 9.9 TRUE))
-- Less than forty: 39.9 qualifies; 40 is a full pension under 3(1)(c), so the person is "eligible for a full monthly pension" and 3(2) does not apply.
#ASSERT `s 3(2): a partial monthly pension may be paid to the person` (`oa1 test: person` (YMD 1961 10 1) `oa1 test: the day of approval` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE 39.9 TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 3(2): a partial monthly pension may be paid to the person` (`oa1 test: person` (YMD 1961 10 1) `oa1 test: the day of approval` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE 40 TRUE))
-- "where that aggregate period is less than twenty years, was resident in Canada on the day preceding": 15 years needs it; 20 years does not.
#ASSERT `s 3(2)(b): the person has resided in Canada for at least ten but less than forty years and, if less than twenty, was resident on the day preceding` (`oa1 test: person` (YMD 1961 10 1) `oa1 test: the day of approval` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE 15 TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 3(2)(b): the person has resided in Canada for at least ten but less than forty years and, if less than twenty, was resident on the day preceding` (`oa1 test: person` (YMD 1961 10 1) `oa1 test: the day of approval` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE 15 FALSE))
#ASSERT `s 3(2)(b): the person has resided in Canada for at least ten but less than forty years and, if less than twenty, was resident on the day preceding` (`oa1 test: person` (YMD 1961 10 1) `oa1 test: the day of approval` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE 20 FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 3(2)(b): the person has resided in Canada for at least ten but less than forty years and, if less than twenty, was resident on the day preceding` (`oa1 test: person` (YMD 1961 10 1) `oa1 test: the day of approval` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE 19.9 FALSE))
-- 3(2)(a): sixty-five. A person of 64 with 15 years does not qualify.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 3(2): a partial monthly pension may be paid to the person` (`oa1 test: person` (YMD 1961 10 2) `oa1 test: the day of approval` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE 15 TRUE))
-- A person qualified for a full pension under 3(1)(a) is not eligible for a partial one, whatever the residence.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 3(2): a partial monthly pension may be paid to the person` (`oa1 test: person` (YMD 1940 1 1) `oa1 test: the day of approval` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE 15 TRUE))

§ `s 4(1): legal residence`

-- The order of the record: pensioner 1977, citizen at approval, legally resident at approval, ceased to reside, citizen when ceased, legally resident when ceased.
-- A pensioner of July 1, 1977 is not held to the requirement ("A person who was not a pensioner ... is eligible ... only if").
#ASSERT `s 4(1): the person meets the requirement of legal residence for a pension under this Part` (`s 4(1): Facts of citizenship and legal residence` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE)
-- (a): a citizen on the day preceding approval; or, if not, legally resident.
#ASSERT `s 4(1): the person meets the requirement of legal residence for a pension under this Part` (`s 4(1): Facts of citizenship and legal residence` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 4(1): the person meets the requirement of legal residence for a pension under this Part` (`s 4(1): Facts of citizenship and legal residence` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE)
-- (b): the person ceased to reside in Canada and was a citizen (or legally resident) on the day preceding that day.
#ASSERT `s 4(1): the person meets the requirement of legal residence for a pension under this Part` (`s 4(1): Facts of citizenship and legal residence` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 4(1): the person meets the requirement of legal residence for a pension under this Part` (`s 4(1): Facts of citizenship and legal residence` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE)
-- Neither (a) nor (b): not eligible. (b) needs the person to have ceased to reside in Canada.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 4(1): the person meets the requirement of legal residence for a pension under this Part` (`s 4(1): Facts of citizenship and legal residence` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 4(1): the person meets the requirement of legal residence for a pension under this Part` (`s 4(1): Facts of citizenship and legal residence` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 4(1): the person meets the requirement of legal residence for a pension under this Part` (`s 4(1): Facts of citizenship and legal residence` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE))

§ `s 4.1: the presumption`

-- The Minister must intend to waive the requirement for an application AND the information must include the prescribed information.
#ASSERT `s 4.1: the presumption applies` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 4.1: the presumption applies` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 4.1: the presumption applies` FALSE TRUE)
-- "presumed, in the absence of evidence to the contrary": evidence to the contrary defeats it.
#ASSERT `s 4.1: the person is presumed to have met the requirements` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 4.1: the person is presumed to have met the requirements` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 4.1: the person is presumed to have met the requirements` FALSE FALSE)
-- (a) and (b): the requirement is treated as met when it is actually met or presumed met.
#ASSERT `s 4.1(a): the requirement of subparagraph 3(1)(b)(iii) or (c)(iii) or paragraph 3(2)(b) is treated as met` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4.1(a): the requirement of subparagraph 3(1)(b)(iii) or (c)(iii) or paragraph 3(2)(b) is treated as met` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 4.1(a): the requirement of subparagraph 3(1)(b)(iii) or (c)(iii) or paragraph 3(2)(b) is treated as met` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 4.1(b): the requirement of paragraph 4(1)(a) or (b) is treated as met` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 4.1(b): the requirement of paragraph 4(1)(a) or (b) is treated as met` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 4.1(b): the requirement of paragraph 4(1)(a) or (b) is treated as met` FALSE FALSE)

§ `s 5(1): limits on payment`

-- Qualified (full by 3(1)(c)), applied for, approved: may be paid.
#ASSERT `s 5(1): a pension may be paid to the person` (`oa1 test: person` (YMD 1961 10 1) `oa1 test: the day of approval` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE 40 TRUE) TRUE TRUE
-- Qualified for a partial pension: may be paid.
#ASSERT `s 5(1): a pension may be paid to the person` (`oa1 test: person` (YMD 1961 10 1) `oa1 test: the day of approval` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE 25 TRUE) TRUE TRUE
-- No application, or not approved, or not qualified: may not.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 5(1): a pension may be paid to the person` (`oa1 test: person` (YMD 1961 10 1) `oa1 test: the day of approval` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE 40 TRUE) FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 5(1): a pension may be paid to the person` (`oa1 test: person` (YMD 1961 10 1) `oa1 test: the day of approval` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE 40 TRUE) TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 5(1): a pension may be paid to the person` (`oa1 test: person` (YMD 1961 10 1) `oa1 test: the day of approval` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 0 FALSE 5 TRUE) TRUE TRUE)
-- Second limb: nothing for a day before the day of approval unless the Act provides otherwise.
#ASSERT `s 5(1): a pension may be paid in respect of the day` (YMD 2026 10 1) `oa1 test: the day of approval` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 5(1): a pension may be paid in respect of the day` (YMD 2026 11 1) `oa1 test: the day of approval` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 5(1): a pension may be paid in respect of the day` (YMD 2026 9 30) `oa1 test: the day of approval` FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 5(1): a pension may be paid in respect of the day` (YMD 2026 9 30) `oa1 test: the day of approval` TRUE

§ `s 5(2): deemed application`

#ASSERT `s 5(2): the application is deemed to have been made and approved` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 5(2): the application is deemed to have been made and approved` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 5(2): the application is deemed to have been made and approved` FALSE TRUE)
-- Born March 15, 1960 reaches sixty-five on March 15, 2025.
#ASSERT `s 5(2): the day on which the person reached sixty-five years of age` (YMD 1960 3 15) EQUALS (YMD 2025 3 15)

§ `s 5(3): incarcerated persons`

`oa1 test: a federal sentence` MEANS `Sentence of imprisonment` OF TRUE, 800, FALSE, FALSE
`oa1 test: a provincial sentence of 91 days under an agreement` MEANS `Sentence of imprisonment` OF FALSE, 91, TRUE, TRUE
`oa1 test: a provincial sentence of 90 days under an agreement` MEANS `Sentence of imprisonment` OF FALSE, 90, TRUE, TRUE
`oa1 test: a provincial sentence of 91 days with no agreement` MEANS `Sentence of imprisonment` OF FALSE, 91, TRUE, FALSE
`oa1 test: a sentence in a place that is not a prison within the Prisons and Reformatories Act` MEANS `Sentence of imprisonment` OF FALSE, 400, FALSE, TRUE

-- (a): a penitentiary sentence. (b): more than 90 days in a prison, with the province's agreement.
#ASSERT `s 5(3): the person is an incarcerated person described in subsection 5(3)` TRUE `oa1 test: a federal sentence`
#ASSERT `s 5(3): the person is an incarcerated person described in subsection 5(3)` TRUE `oa1 test: a provincial sentence of 91 days under an agreement`
#ASSERT NOT (`s 5(3): the person is an incarcerated person described in subsection 5(3)` TRUE `oa1 test: a provincial sentence of 90 days under an agreement`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 5(3): the person is an incarcerated person described in subsection 5(3)` TRUE `oa1 test: a provincial sentence of 91 days with no agreement`)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 5(3): the person is an incarcerated person described in subsection 5(3)` TRUE `oa1 test: a sentence in a place that is not a prison within the Prisons and Reformatories Act`)
-- A person who is not incarcerated is not an incarcerated person, whatever the sentence.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 5(3): the person is an incarcerated person described in subsection 5(3)` FALSE `oa1 test: a federal sentence`)

-- The months barred: incarcerated from March 10, 2026, released June 20, 2026. The first month (March) is excluded from the bar;
-- April and May are barred; June, the month of release, is paid (ss 8(2.1), 9.2); July is after the period.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 5(3): no pension may be paid for the month` (YMD 2026 3 20) TRUE (YMD 2026 3 10) (JUST (YMD 2026 6 20)))
#ASSERT `s 5(3): no pension may be paid for the month` (YMD 2026 4 1) TRUE (YMD 2026 3 10) (JUST (YMD 2026 6 20))
#ASSERT `s 5(3): no pension may be paid for the month` (YMD 2026 5 31) TRUE (YMD 2026 3 10) (JUST (YMD 2026 6 20))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 5(3): no pension may be paid for the month` (YMD 2026 6 1) TRUE (YMD 2026 3 10) (JUST (YMD 2026 6 20)))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 5(3): no pension may be paid for the month` (YMD 2026 7 1) TRUE (YMD 2026 3 10) (JUST (YMD 2026 6 20)))
-- Not yet released: every month after the first is barred. A person not described is never barred.
#ASSERT `s 5(3): no pension may be paid for the month` (YMD 2027 1 1) TRUE (YMD 2026 3 10) NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT (`s 5(3): no pension may be paid for the month` (YMD 2026 4 1) FALSE (YMD 2026 3 10) NOTHING)

§ `s 5.1: withdrawal`

#ASSERT `s 5.1(1): the applicant may withdraw the application` TRUE (YMD 2026 10 31) (YMD 2026 11 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 5.1(1): the applicant may withdraw the application` TRUE (YMD 2026 11 1) (YMD 2026 11 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 5.1(1): the applicant may withdraw the application` TRUE (YMD 2026 11 2) (YMD 2026 11 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 5.1(1): the applicant may withdraw the application` FALSE (YMD 2026 10 31) (YMD 2026 11 1))
-- Used until the withdrawal, not after.
#ASSERT `s 5.1(2): the application may be used to determine the applicant's eligibility on the day` (YMD 2026 12 1) NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 5.1(2): the application may be used to determine the applicant's eligibility on the day` (YMD 2026 10 31) (JUST (YMD 2026 10 31))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 5.1(2): the application may be used to determine the applicant's eligibility on the day` (YMD 2026 11 1) (JUST (YMD 2026 10 31)))

§ `s 6: census information`

-- A census taken more than thirty years before the request: October 1, 1996 is exactly thirty years before October 1, 2026, not "more than".
#ASSERT `s 6: the Minister is entitled to obtain the information from Statistics Canada on request` TRUE TRUE (YMD 1990 4 1) (YMD 2026 10 1) TRUE
#ASSERT `s 6: the Minister is entitled to obtain the information from Statistics Canada on request` TRUE TRUE (YMD 1996 9 30) (YMD 2026 10 1) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 6: the Minister is entitled to obtain the information from Statistics Canada on request` TRUE TRUE (YMD 1996 10 1) (YMD 2026 10 1) TRUE)
-- The regulations' conditions, the subject (age) and the census source are each required.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 6: the Minister is entitled to obtain the information from Statistics Canada on request` TRUE TRUE (YMD 1990 4 1) (YMD 2026 10 1) FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 6: the Minister is entitled to obtain the information from Statistics Canada on request` FALSE TRUE (YMD 1990 4 1) (YMD 2026 10 1) TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 6: the Minister is entitled to obtain the information from Statistics Canada on request` TRUE FALSE (YMD 1990 4 1) (YMD 2026 10 1) TRUE)
